      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/PublicAdministrationBusinessActor"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/PublicAdministrationBusinessActor"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:PublicAdministrationBusinessActor"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Public Administration Business-actor"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA team"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="1. Implementing Tax Regulations: Public Administration plays a crucial role in implementing tax regulations. They ensure that all individuals and businesses comply with the tax laws and pay their taxes correctly and on time. They also handle any disputes or issues related to taxes.&#xA;&#xA;2. Tax Collection: Public Administration is responsible for collecting taxes from individuals and businesses. They manage the process of tax collection and ensure that all taxes are collected efficiently and effectively.&#xA;&#xA;3. Tax Policy Development: Public Administration is involved in the development of tax policies. They analyze the economic conditions and propose changes to the tax policies to meet the economic goals of the country.&#xA;&#xA;4. Tax Auditing: Public Administration conducts audits to ensure that taxes are being paid correctly. They check the financial records of individuals and businesses to ensure that they are not evading taxes.&#xA;&#xA;5. Tax Education: Public Administration educates the public about tax laws and regulations. They provide information and guidance to individuals and businesses to help them understand their tax obligations.&#xA;&#xA;6. Tax Enforcement: Public Administration enforces tax laws. They investigate and prosecute cases of tax evasion and fraud.&#xA;&#xA;7. Tax Legislation: Public Administration plays a role in the creation of tax legislation. They work with lawmakers to draft and pass tax laws.&#xA;&#xA;8. Tax Planning: Public Administration is involved in tax planning. They help to forecast tax revenues and plan for the use of these funds in the budget.&#xA;&#xA;9. Tax Dispute Resolution: Public Administration resolves disputes related to taxes. They mediate between the tax authorities and taxpayers to resolve any disagreements or issues.&#xA;&#xA;10. Tax Research: Public Administration conducts research on tax issues. They study trends, analyze data, and provide insights to help improve tax policies and practices."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Public Administration role is a crucial entity in the European Taxes Regulation framework, responsible for the execution and enforcement of laws, regulations, and policies related to taxation. As an ArchiMate business role, it represents a specific way of performing an organizational behavior, which is defined by a set of responsibilities, competencies, and obligations.&#xA;&#xA;In the context of European Taxes Regulation, the Public Administration role involves the collection of taxes from individuals and businesses in accordance with European Union tax laws and regulations. This includes the administration of tax codes, the assessment and collection of taxes, and the enforcement of tax compliance. &#xA;&#xA;The role is also responsible for the interpretation and application of tax laws and regulations, ensuring that they are applied fairly and consistently across all taxpayers. This involves providing guidance and advice to taxpayers, resolving disputes and issues related to tax compliance, and conducting audits to ensure that taxes are being paid correctly.&#xA;&#xA;Moreover, the Public Administration role plays a key role in the development and implementation of tax policies and strategies. This includes the analysis of tax trends and issues, the development of proposals for tax reform, and the implementation of tax policies and strategies to support economic growth and fiscal stability.&#xA;&#xA;In addition, the role is responsible for the management and allocation of public funds, ensuring that they are used effectively and efficiently to deliver public services and achieve policy objectives. This involves the planning, budgeting, and monitoring of public expenditure, as well as the management of public assets and liabilities.&#xA;&#xA;Furthermore, the Public Administration role is involved in the coordination and cooperation with other public authorities and stakeholders, both at the national and European level, to ensure a coherent and effective approach to tax administration and policy-making.&#xA;&#xA;In the ArchiMate language, the Public Administration role is typically modeled as a business role that interacts with other business roles, business processes, and business objects in the tax regulation domain. This allows for a clear representation of the role's responsibilities and interactions in the context of the overall business architecture."/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="The Public Administration role is responsible for the implementation, management, and enforcement of European tax regulations. This includes the collection of taxes, ensuring compliance with tax laws, and the administration of tax-related services. They are also tasked with the interpretation and application of tax laws and regulations, providing guidance and support to taxpayers, and conducting audits to prevent and detect tax evasion. As an Archimate business role, they are also involved in the strategic planning, decision-making, and policy-making processes related to tax administration."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Digital Public Service Consumers"/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="taxes"/>
