    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Permission Policy" id="id-4afab44446d44bc3b30cc6a23fc954e3">
      <documentation>Definition: A permission policy can be defined as a set of rules, guidelines, and controls that govern the authorization and access rights granted to individuals or roles within a system or organization. It outlines the specific permissions and privileges assigned to different entities to ensure appropriate access control and maintain the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of resources or information.

Source: ENISA

Source reference: https://resilience.enisa.europa.eu/article-13/guideline-for-minimum-security-measures/Article_13a_ENISA_Technical_Guideline_On_Security_Measures_v2_0.pdf

LOST view: SV-Governance Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/PermissionPolicyBusinessObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataPolicy

ABB name: egovera:PermissionPolicyBusinessObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-16-01

</documentation>
