    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Data Quality Framework" id="id-9480481a764347d0bd39e4b0b9d6c575">
      <documentation>Definition: A Data Quality Framework refers to a structured approach or set of guidelines that organizations use to assess, measure, and improve the quality of their data. It provides a systematic framework for managing data quality throughout its lifecycle, from data collection to data analysis and decision-making.

Source: European Commission

LOST view: SV-Governance Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataQualityFrameworkBusinessObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataPolicy

ABB name: egovera:DataQualityFrameworkBusinessObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-16-01

</documentation>
