      <property key="skos:definition" value="A Public Policy Officer is responsible for analyzing, developing, and implementing policies related to public issues for an organization or government entity. They conduct research, gather data, and monitor legislation to understand its impact on their organization. They also liaise with stakeholders, including government officials, to advocate for their organization's interests. Their role may also involve educating the public or their organization about relevant policies and legislation."/>
