    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Tangible assets registry management for properties" id="id-04bcf6656ff24e509947ecced337a026">
      <documentation>Definition: Tangible Assets (Properties) Registry Management refers to the use of IT systems and software to record, track, manage, and analyze the physical assets owned by an organization or individual. These assets can include buildings, land, machinery, vehicles, and other physical properties.

Source: Investopedia

Source reference: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tangibleasset.asp

Additional information: Tangible Assets (Properties) Registry Management systems are crucial for businesses and organizations as they provide a comprehensive overview of the company's physical assets. These systems can track the location, quantity, condition, maintenance schedules, and other important details of each asset. They can also assist in calculating depreciation, managing asset lifecycles, and planning for future asset purchases or disposals. The use of such systems can lead to improved asset utilization, cost savings, and better decision-making.

Example: Examples of application include a real estate company using a Tangible Assets Registry Management system to keep track of all its properties, their locations, values, and maintenance schedules. Another example could be a manufacturing company using the system to manage its machinery and equipment, tracking their usage, maintenance needs, and depreciation over time.

LOST view: OV-Digital Public Services Catalogue

