    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Environmental Tax calculation and payment" id="id-31b968073e1242029cae159a018d1499">
      <documentation>Definition: The Environmental Tax Calculation and Payment IT Concept refers to the use of information technology systems and software to calculate and process payments for environmental taxes. These taxes are levied on businesses and individuals for their environmental impact, such as carbon emissions, waste production, and resource consumption.

Source: Investopedia

Source reference: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/environmental-tax.asp

Additional information: The Environmental Tax Calculation and Payment IT Concept involves the use of digital tools to automate the process of calculating and paying environmental taxes. This can include software that tracks a company's carbon emissions and calculates the corresponding tax, or online platforms that allow individuals to pay their environmental taxes. These systems can help ensure accuracy and compliance, reduce administrative burden, and provide valuable data for environmental policy and planning. They can also support the principle of 'polluter pays' by ensuring that those who cause environmental harm bear the cost.

Example: An example of the Environmental Tax Calculation and Payment IT Concept is a software used by a manufacturing company to track its carbon emissions. The software calculates the company's environmental tax based on these emissions and generates a report for tax filing. Another example is an online platform that allows individuals to calculate and pay their environmental taxes based on their household energy consumption and waste production.

LOST view: OV-Digital Public Services Catalogue

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EnvironmentalTaxCalculationAndPaymentBusinessService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalPublicBusinessService

