      <property key="skos:definition" value="Patrimony Analysis is an IT concept that refers to the process of evaluating and managing the entire set of assets (tangible or intangible) owned by an organization. This includes software, hardware, data, and intellectual property. It helps in understanding the value, usage, and lifecycle of these assets, thereby aiding in strategic decision-making."/>
