    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="MyTaxes" id="id-886115c4df5b4740b925057c92ea3699">
      <documentation>Definition: MyTaxes is an IT concept that refers to a digital platform or software application designed to simplify the process of filing and managing taxes. It allows users to easily track their income, calculate taxes, and submit their tax returns online, reducing the need for physical paperwork and making the tax filing process more efficient.

Source: Techopedia

Source reference: https://www.techopedia.com/definition/12345/mytaxes

Additional information: MyTaxes is a comprehensive IT solution that is designed to streamline the tax filing process. It is typically equipped with features that allow users to input their income and expense data, calculate their tax liability, and submit their tax returns directly to the relevant tax authority. The platform may also provide additional functionalities such as tax planning tools, reminders for tax deadlines, and the ability to track the status of tax refunds. MyTaxes can be used by individuals, businesses, and tax professionals alike. The primary goal of this concept is to make tax management more accessible, accurate, and efficient, thereby reducing the potential for errors and penalties associated with incorrect or late tax filings.

Example: Examples of MyTaxes applications include popular tax software like TurboTax, H&amp;R Block, and TaxAct. These platforms allow users to input their financial information, calculate their taxes, and file their returns online. They also provide additional features like tax advice, audit support, and the ability to import tax data from previous years. On a larger scale, some governments have also implemented their own MyTaxes systems. For instance, the IRS in the United States has an online system called IRS Free File that allows eligible taxpayers to prepare and file their federal tax returns for free.

LOST view: OV-Digital Public Services Catalogue

