    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Tax calendar" id="id-a7e8d31e78494292a18e2c135b688267">
      <documentation>Definition: Tax Calendar is an IT concept that refers to a system or software that helps individuals or businesses to manage their tax obligations. It provides reminders for important tax dates, deadlines, and obligations to ensure compliance with tax laws and avoid penalties.

Source: Investopedia

Source reference: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tax-calendar.asp

Additional information: A Tax Calendar is a comprehensive tool that helps in managing and planning tax-related activities. It is designed to keep track of tax deadlines and obligations, making it easier for businesses and individuals to stay compliant with tax laws. The calendar may include dates for filing tax returns, making tax payments, and other tax-related activities. It is especially useful for businesses with complex tax obligations, as it helps to simplify tax management and reduce the risk of missing deadlines. The Tax Calendar can be integrated with other financial systems or software to provide a holistic view of financial obligations.

Example: 1. A small business may use a Tax Calendar to keep track of various tax deadlines, such as the due dates for quarterly estimated tax payments and annual tax return filings. 2. An individual taxpayer may use a Tax Calendar to remind them of the deadline for filing their personal income tax return. 3. A multinational corporation may use a Tax Calendar to manage tax obligations in different jurisdictions, ensuring that they meet all local, state, national, and international tax deadlines.

LOST view: OV-Digital Public Services Catalogue

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TaxCalendarBusinessService

