    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Artificial Intelligence" id="id-d6f8f780cb374cc79c1aa4ccf3bd4b29">
      <documentation>Definition: Artificial intelligence (AI) is intelligence—perceiving, synthesizing, and inferring information—demonstrated by machines, as opposed to intelligence displayed by humans or by other animals

Source: WikiPedia

Source reference: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence

Additional information: Artificial Intelligence is a multidisciplinary field that combines machine learning, natural language processing, robotics, cognitive computing, and more. It's about creating machines that can think and learn like humans. AI systems are designed to handle tasks such as recognizing speech, identifying images, making decisions, and translating languages. They can be classified into two main types: narrow AI, which is designed to perform a narrow task (e.g. facial recognition or internet searches), and general AI, which can perform any intellectual task that a human being can do.

Example: [object Object]

LOST view: Organisational view [Motivation]

