    <element xsi:type="archimate:Contract" name="Multilateral agreements on tax information exchange" id="id-5045226d0e734e6ca78ef661bfecf349">
      <documentation>DESCRIPTION:&#xD;
Multilateral agreement providing a standardised and efficient mechanism to facilitate the automatic exchange of tax information.</documentation>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="https://www.oecd.org/tax/exchange-of-tax-information/convention-on-mutual-administrative-assistance-in-tax-matters.htm"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Multilateral agreements on tax information exchange"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The Multilateral Convention on Mutual Administrative Assistance in Tax Matters is a comprehensive multilateral instrument available for all forms of tax co-operation to tackle tax evasion and avoidance, a top priority for all countries. The Convention was developed jointly by the OECD and the Council of Europe in 1988 and amended in 2010 to respond to the call by the G20 to align it to the international standard on information exchange."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD)"/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="https://www.oecd.org/tax/exchange-of-tax-information/convention-on-mutual-administrative-assistance-in-tax-matters.htm"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="1. Exchange of information on request: A country can request another country to provide specific information about a taxpayer's financial and tax status.,2. Spontaneous exchange of information: A country can voluntarily provide information to another country about a taxpayer's financial and tax status.,3. Automatic exchange of information: Countries can systematically and periodically exchange taxpayer information.,4. Simultaneous tax examinations: Two or more countries can agree to simultaneously examine the affairs of a taxpayer to ensure compliance with tax laws.,5. Assistance in recovery of tax claims: A country can request another country to help recover tax claims from a taxpayer."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Convention provides for all possible forms of administrative co-operation between states in the assessment and collection of taxes, in particular with a view to combating tax avoidance and evasion. This co-operation ranges from exchange of information, including automatic exchanges, to the recovery of foreign tax claims."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Legal Agreements"/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Legal"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="taxes"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalAgreementContract"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Contract" name="Code of Conduct for Energy Efficiency in Data Centres" id="id-521ebc1717934898848ddc1c747c86e9">
      <documentation>Description: This voluntary code of conduct was developed by the European Commission's Joint Research Centre to improve the energy efficiency and environmental sustainability of data centers. It provides guidelines and best practices for data center operators to reduce their environmental impact.

Additional information: The European Code of Conduct for Data Centres is a voluntary initiative managed by the Joint Research Centre (JRC), the European Commission’s science and knowledge service. It primarily addresses data centre owners and operators, and secondly the supply chain and service providers. The Code of Conduct aims to reduce energy consumption in data centres in a cost-effective manner without hampering their critical function.

Example: A data centre operator could conduct an energy audit to identify areas where energy is being wasted. For example, they might find that their servers are using more power than necessary during off-peak hours. Based on these findings, they could create an Action Plan to reduce energy usage, such as implementing server virtualization to consolidate workloads and reduce the number of physical servers needed, or using energy-efficient cooling systems.

Publisher: Joint Research Centre

Source: https://joint-research-centre.ec.europa.eu/scientific-activities-z/energy-efficiency/energy-efficiency-products/code-conduct-ict/code-conduct-energy-efficiency-data-centres_en

LOST view: OV-Data Spaces

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CodeOfConductForEnergyEfficiencyInDataCentresContract

EIRA traceability: eira:OrganisationalAgreementContract

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-07

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CodeOfConductForEnergyEfficiencyInDataCentresContract

dct:title: Code of Conduct for Energy Efficiency in Data Centres

</documentation>
