    <element xsi:type="archimate:Representation" name="RDF Serialisations" id="id-434fd0bf39a84ff3b86a7910a4c820b9">
      <documentation>Definition: RDF serialization can be defined as the process of encoding RDF (Resource Description Framework) data into a specific format or syntax that enables the storage, transmission, and exchange of structured data in a machine-readable manner. It involves transforming RDF triples into a serialized form, allowing data to be easily parsed, interpreted, and processed by both humans and computer systems.

Source: W3C

Source reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf11-primer/

LOST view: SV-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFSerialisationsRepresentation

EIRA traceability: eira:DataRepresentation

ABB name: egovera:RDFSerialisationsRepresentation

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-16-01

</documentation>
