    <element xsi:type="archimate:Representation" name="N3" id="id-6f0a25641a6241b281f4977cdeb053e6">
      <documentation>Description: N3 is a serialization format for representing RDF (Resource Description Framework) data. It is an extension of Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) and provides additional features for expressing rules, formulas, and logical statements within RDF graphs. N3 aims to provide a more expressive and flexible syntax for representing RDF data compared to other serialization formats.

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TeamSubmission/n3/

LOST view: SV-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/N3Representation

EIRA traceability: eira:DataRepresentation

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-08-20

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/N3Representation

</documentation>
