    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="Geo-Localization" id="id-f504f6a700dc4cb9aadec8369b0326a8">
      <documentation>Definition: The Geo-localization Application Service is a web service that provides functionality for determining and retrieving the geographic location of a device, user, or point of interest using various data sources and techniques. It enables applications to integrate location-based features and services, such as mapping, routing, proximity search, and geofencing, into their functionality. The Geo-localization Application Service utilizes a combination of technologies, including GPS, IP geolocation, Wi-Fi positioning, cellular network data, and geospatial algorithms, to accurately determine and track the location information. It offers a standardized and accessible interface for developers to query and utilize location data in their applications, allowing for enhanced user experiences, targeted services, and location-aware functionality

Source: European Location Framework (ELF)

Source reference: https://www.elfproject.eu/

LOST view: TVA-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface

EIRA traceability: eira:WebServiceApplicationInterface

ABB name: egovera:Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-01-18

</documentation>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
