      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/IntelIONOSOrbiterConnectorApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-28"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/IntelIONOSOrbiterConnectorApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector Application Service"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector could be used to connect a data space for automotive data with a data space for energy data. This would allow for the sharing of data about vehicle emissions and energy consumption, which could be used to improve the efficiency of transportation systems."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="It is based on the Eclipse Dataspace Connector (EDC) specification, which is an open standard for connecting data spaces. It is designed to be interoperable with other EDC-compliant connectors, allowing for the secure and federated sharing of data across different data spaces.It is implemented in Java and can be deployed on a variety of platforms, including on-premises servers, cloud platforms, and edge devices. It is available as a free and open source software project. The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector is a valuable tool for organizations that need to share data securely and efficiently across different data spaces. It is easy to use and deploy, and it is compatible with a wide range of platforms."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector is an implementation of the Eclipse Dataspace Connector (EDC) specification. It is designed to be interoperable with other EDC-compliant connectors, allowing for the secure and federated sharing of data across different data spaces."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="Intel"/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/homepage.html"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="TVA-Data Space Enablers [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Sovity Dataspace Connector" id="id-2182709c4ecc47f6aef2756164017aba">
      <documentation>Description: A software component that enables data sharing and data sovereignty based on the EDC framework and the IDS standard.

Additional information: The Sovity Dataspace Connector is an extension of the EDC Connector, which provides a framework for sovereign, inter-organizational data exchange. Sovity adds features such as easy access, automated integration, simple usage, fully managed services, and data space expertise to offer enterprise-ready solutions for data sharing. Sovity also provides different editions of the connector, such as the Community Edition, which contains pre-configured open source extensions.

Example: An example of the Sovity Dataspace Connector in action is a consortium of healthcare providers sharing patient data securely and efficiently. The connector enables the seamless exchange of patient records, medical images, and diagnostic reports between hospitals, clinics, and research institutions. It ensures that sensitive patient information is protected and accessed only by authorized entities, while allowing healthcare professionals to collaborate and make informed decisions based on comprehensive and up-to-date patient data. The connector also facilitates the integration of data from wearable devices, remote monitoring systems, and electronic health records, enabling a holistic view of patient health and supporting personalized medicine initiatives.

Publisher: Sovity

Source: https://sovity.de/

LOST view: TVA-Data Space Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SovityDataspaceConnectorApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-20

