    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Surveillance system (import declaration and eCommerce)" id="id-303e19acc1c54f53a3e97e0fc2b5d9a2">
      <documentation>Description: It represents the use or consumption of features provided by a surveillance system allowing private and public Organization to monitor Import and Declaration from one country to another.

Additional information: The surveillance system for import declaration and eCommerce is a comprehensive tool that enables both private and public organizations to oversee and manage the import and declaration process from one country to another. This system is particularly useful in the realm of eCommerce, where goods are frequently shipped across international borders. The system can track and monitor these transactions, ensuring that all necessary customs and import regulations are being followed. It can also help to prevent fraud and smuggling, as well as to ensure that all taxes and duties are being properly paid. The system may include features such as real-time tracking, data analysis, and reporting tools.

Example: An example of the application of this system could be an eCommerce platform like Amazon, which ships goods internationally. The surveillance system would monitor all transactions, ensuring that all goods are properly declared and that all customs regulations are being followed. It could also be used by a government customs agency to monitor imports and exports, ensuring compliance with all relevant laws and regulations.

Publisher: Customs and Border Protection

Source: https://www.cbp.gov/trade/automated

LOST view: TVA-Tax Management Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SurveillanceSystemApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

