      <property key="skos:note" value="The Excise Movement and Control System (EMCS) is a computerised system that monitors the movement of excise goods under suspension of duty within the EU. It is used to ensure that excise duties are correctly applied and paid for goods such as alcohol, tobacco, and energy products. The system records the movement of these goods in real-time, providing a transparent and efficient means of control for tax authorities. It also helps to prevent fraud and smuggling by providing a traceable record of the movement of goods."/>
