    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Tax calendar management service" id="id-82eb6e9beaf4492da1bc49158b604780">
      <documentation>Definition: Tax Calendar Management Service is the utilization of features provided by a calendar management system to identify and manage the different taxes deadlines and milestones in a tax year. A tax year is the annual accounting period for paying or withholding taxes, keeping records, and reporting income and expenses.

Source: Self-Generated

Source reference: N/A

Additional information: Tax Calendar Management Service is a crucial tool for businesses and individuals to ensure timely compliance with tax obligations. It provides a systematic approach to manage tax-related deadlines and milestones throughout the tax year. This service can include features like reminders for upcoming deadlines, tracking of tax payments, and organization of tax-related documents. It can also assist in planning for future tax obligations, helping to avoid penalties for late or missed payments. The service can be customized to suit the specific tax requirements of the user, making it a versatile tool for tax management.

Example: 1. A small business owner uses a Tax Calendar Management Service to keep track of quarterly tax payments and annual tax return deadlines. The service sends reminders for upcoming deadlines and helps the owner organize tax-related documents.
2. An individual taxpayer uses a Tax Calendar Management Service to manage their personal income tax obligations. The service provides reminders for important dates like the last day to contribute to an IRA for the tax year, the deadline for filing a tax return, and the due dates for estimated tax payments.

LOST view: TVA-Tax Management Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TaxCalendarManagementServiceApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:TaxCalendarManagementServiceApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-28

