      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-28"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Apache NiFi Application Service"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="An example application of Apache NiFi is in a data lake architecture. NiFi can be used to ingest data from various sources like sensors, social media feeds, and databases into a centralized data lake. It can then perform data transformations, filtering, and enrichment before storing the processed data in a suitable format for downstream analytics. NiFi's visual interface makes it easy to design and manage complex data flows, ensuring efficient and reliable data movement within the data lake ecosystem."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="Apache NiFi is designed to handle real-time data streaming and batch processing, making it suitable for use cases such as IoT data collection, log aggregation, data migration, and data transformation. It provides a scalable and reliable platform for managing data flows across various systems, including databases, cloud storage, messaging systems, and more. NiFi's GUI allows users to visually create and modify data pipelines, making it accessible to both technical and non-technical users. It offers features like data provenance, security, data lineage, and extensive monitoring capabilities. NiFi also supports data governance and compliance requirements through features like data encryption, access control, and auditing."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="Apache NiFi is an open-source data integration and data flow automation tool that provides a visual interface to easily manage and control the movement of data between different systems. It allows users to design, build, and execute data flows, known as data pipelines, using a web-based graphical user interface (GUI). NiFi supports a wide range of data sources, destinations, and processors, enabling efficient data ingestion, transformation, routing, and monitoring."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="Apache NiFi - Official Website"/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="https://nifi.apache.org/"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="TVA-Data Management Enablers [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Accounting" id="id-91f85fcede8642bc90b62a5d416b8954">
      <documentation>Definition: Accounting ABB is an Application Service that enables the process of tracking and recording access to resources, facilities and information.

Source: Inspired in Springer (Authentication, Authorization and Accounting article)

Source reference: https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-52829-4_14

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): BASICAL system was developed by the General Administration Intervention Board to give computer support to operations and information in the basic model of the Accounting Information System for Local Governments, in compliance with Order EHA/404/2004, of 23 November, approving the Basic Local Accounting Model Regulations. https://administracionelectronica.gob.es/ctt/verPestanaGeneralAbstract.htm?idIniciativa=basical#.ZAISY3bMI2w

IoP Dimension: Behavioral IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Interoperability saliency: The Accounting Application Service ABB is salient for interoperability because it can be a mechanism to track and control access to data, applications, and services. This can help to identify when unauthorised changes or accesses have been accepted and data in a digital public servicer has been compromised and whom is the actor involved. 

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/AccountingApplicationService

eira:ID: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/AccountingApplicationService

ABB name: eira:AccountingApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-18-01

</documentation>
