    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Digital Collaboration" id="id-c3c5980a11d84be69d901b15d0903323">
      <documentation>LOST view: TVA-Digital Workplace Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DigitalCollaborationApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:DigitalCollaborationApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-18-01

</documentation>
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DigitalCollaborationApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DigitalCollaborationApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Digital Collaboration Application Service"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:DigitalCollaborationApplicationService"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="Digital collaboration refers to the use of digital tools and platforms to work together with others in a virtual environment. It involves the sharing of information, ideas, and resources to achieve common goals or complete tasks, regardless of the physical location of the participants."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="Techopedia"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference" value="https://www.techopedia.com/definition/3805/collaboration"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="Using Zoom or Microsoft Teams to hold virtual meetings with team members located in different cities or countries.&#xA;Utilizing Google Docs or Microsoft OneDrive to collaboratively edit documents in real-time, allowing multiple users to make changes simultaneously.&#xA;Employing tools like Asana, Trello, or Jira to track project progress, assign tasks, and manage deadlines across a team.&#xA;Leveraging Slack or Microsoft Teams for quick communication and to facilitate discussions in dedicated channels for different topics or projects.&#xA;Using Office 365 or G Suite to access a comprehensive set of tools that support various aspects of collaboration, including email, calendaring, file storage, and more."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="Digital collaboration encompasses a wide range of technologies and practices, including but not limited to, video conferencing, cloud-based document and file sharing, project management applications, instant messaging, and collaborative software suites that integrate multiple functions. These tools enable individuals and teams to communicate in real-time or asynchronously, enhancing productivity and facilitating the exchange of knowledge. Effective digital collaboration requires not only the right tools but also a culture that promotes open communication, trust, and the willingness to share expertise. As remote work and distributed teams become more prevalent, digital collaboration is increasingly critical for maintaining team cohesion and ensuring successful project outcomes."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="skos:broader" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Tax customer messaging solution" id="id-c4b941e9574c448e84a1c2216236a271">
      <documentation>Definition: A Tax Customer Messaging Solution refers to the use or consumption of features provided by a customer messaging solution that enables remote interaction with the customer through various messaging platforms. This solution is often used in the tax industry to facilitate communication between tax professionals and their clients.

Source: Assistant's Knowledge

Source reference: N/A

Additional information: The Tax Customer Messaging Solution is a crucial tool in today's digital age, especially in the tax industry. It allows tax professionals to interact with their clients remotely, providing a platform for discussions, clarifications, and updates regarding tax-related matters. This solution may include features such as automated responses, personalized messages, real-time communication, and more. It can be integrated into various messaging platforms, making it a versatile and flexible tool for enhancing customer service and engagement. Moreover, it can also help in improving the efficiency and productivity of tax professionals by streamlining the communication process.

Example: 1. A tax professional using a Tax Customer Messaging Solution to send automated reminders to their clients about upcoming tax deadlines. 
2. A tax firm integrating this solution into their system to provide real-time responses to client inquiries regarding their tax returns. 
3. A tax consultant using this solution to send personalized messages to their clients, providing them with updates and advice on their tax situation.

LOST view: TVA-Tax Management Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TaxCustomerMessagingSolutionApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:TaxCustomerMessagingSolutionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-28

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TaxCustomerMessagingSolutionApplicationService

dct:title: Tax Customer Messaging Solution Application Service

</documentation>
