    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="EBSI Wallet For Holders" id="id-f32705dbc80143469fb348bd116b01c1">
      <documentation>Description: The EBSI Wallet for Holders is designed to empower users by allowing them to manage their Verifiable Credentials (VCs) efficiently and securely. Under the EBSI (European Blockchain Services Infrastructure) Verifiable Credentials exchange framework, the Wallet for Holders offers a suite of functionalities that cater specifically to the needs of credential holders. Request Issuance of Verifiable Credentials: Users can initiate requests for the issuance of VCs from trusted issuers. This functionality ensures that individuals can easily obtain credentials that validate their identity, qualifications, or other attributes.

Example: The following narrative is ficticius example that can help to understand how EUDI Wallet can be used: Maria, an EU citizen, needs to access healthcare services in another EU country. Using her EUDI Wallet, she logs in with her secure credentials. The healthcare provider requests her health insurance information, and Maria consents to share it through the wallet. The EUDI Wallet securely transmits her insurance details, allowing the provider to validate and authorize her access to services. This seamless process ensures that Maria receives the necessary healthcare without any physical paperwork, showcasing the EUDI Wallet's efficiency in managing identity verification, secure data sharing, and cross-border access. 

Publisher: European Commission

Source: EBSI

LOST view: TVA-Identification and Access Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EUDIWalletForHoldersApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EUDIWalletForHoldersApplicationService

Name: EUDI Wallet For Holders

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentificationApplicationService

</documentation>
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EUDIWalletForHoldersApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-28"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EUDIWalletForHoldersApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="EUDI Wallet For Holders"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="The following narrative is ficticius example that can help to understand how EUDI Wallet can be used: Maria, an EU citizen, needs to access healthcare services in another EU country. Using her EUDI Wallet, she logs in with her secure credentials. The healthcare provider requests her health insurance information, and Maria consents to share it through the wallet. The EUDI Wallet securely transmits her insurance details, allowing the provider to validate and authorize her access to services. This seamless process ensures that Maria receives the necessary healthcare without any physical paperwork, showcasing the EUDI Wallet's efficiency in managing identity verification, secure data sharing, and cross-border access. "/>
      <property key="skos:note"/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The EBSI Wallet for Holders is designed to empower users by allowing them to manage their Verifiable Credentials (VCs) efficiently and securely. Under the EBSI (European Blockchain Services Infrastructure) Verifiable Credentials exchange framework, the Wallet for Holders offers a suite of functionalities that cater specifically to the needs of credential holders. Request Issuance of Verifiable Credentials: Users can initiate requests for the issuance of VCs from trusted issuers. This functionality ensures that individuals can easily obtain credentials that validate their identity, qualifications, or other attributes."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="European Commission"/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="EBSI"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="TVA-Identification and Access Enablers [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentificationApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Smart queue management" id="id-f476256ded864773891f6b36dc857b6f">
      <documentation>Definition: Smart Queue Management is a digital service that uses advanced algorithms and data analysis to manage and optimize the flow of customers or users in a queue. This service can be used in various sectors such as retail, healthcare, and transportation to improve efficiency and customer satisfaction.

Source: Techopedia

Source reference: https://www.techopedia.com/definition/31575/queue-management-system

Additional information: Smart Queue Management is a technology-driven solution that helps businesses manage customer flow effectively. It uses real-time data and predictive analytics to estimate waiting times, streamline the queuing process, and improve service efficiency. This system can be integrated with digital signage to display queue information and wait times, enhancing the customer experience. It can also provide valuable insights into customer behavior and peak times, enabling businesses to allocate resources more effectively. Moreover, it can reduce physical queues, making it particularly useful in the context of social distancing measures.

Example: In a retail setting, a smart queue management system can be used to manage queues at checkouts, reducing wait times and improving customer satisfaction. It can also provide data on peak times, helping the store to allocate staff more effectively.

In a healthcare setting, such as a hospital or clinic, smart queue management can be used to manage patient flow, reducing wait times and improving patient satisfaction. It can also provide data on peak times, helping the hospital to allocate staff and resources more effectively.

In a transportation setting, such as an airport or train station, smart queue management can be used to manage passenger flow, reducing wait times and improving passenger satisfaction. It can also provide data on peak times, helping the airport or station to allocate staff and resources more effectively.

LOST view: TVA-Analytics Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SmartQueueManagementApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:SmartQueueManagementApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-08-16

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SmartQueueManagementApplicationService

dct:title: Smart Queue Management Application Service

</documentation>
