    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Local tax authorities" id="id-09188746c9114ca2a30c857d3491b4d6">
      <documentation>Definition: Local tax authorities are government agencies at the local level responsible for assessing, levying, and collecting taxes within their jurisdiction. They ensure the enforcement of tax laws and regulations, provide tax-related services to taxpayers, and manage the revenue collected from taxes.

Source: Investopedia

Source reference: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tax-authority.asp

Additional information: Local tax authorities play a crucial role in the financial ecosystem of a region. They are responsible for the collection of various types of taxes such as property tax, sales tax, income tax, etc., depending on the tax laws of the region. These authorities ensure that individuals and businesses comply with local tax laws and pay their due taxes. They also provide services such as tax assistance, dispute resolution, and tax education to taxpayers. The revenue collected by these authorities is used to fund local government services and initiatives, such as public education, infrastructure development, and public safety.

Example: [object Object],[object Object],[object Object]

LOST view: SV-Datasets Catalogue [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/LocalTaxAuthoritiesDataObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataSetCatalogueDataObject

ABB name: egovera:LocalTaxAuthoritiesDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-27

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/LocalTaxAuthoritiesDataObject

dct:title: Local Tax Authorities

</documentation>
