      <property key="skos:note" value="The WTO Trade and Goods Exchange Metadata is a crucial resource for economists, policymakers, and researchers studying international trade. It provides a detailed picture of the flow of goods and services between countries, allowing for in-depth analysis of trade patterns, trends, and impacts. The data is collected from official sources in each WTO member country and is standardized to ensure comparability. It covers a wide range of goods and services, from agricultural products to high-tech goods and services. The metadata includes information on the quantity and value of goods and services traded, the countries involved in the trade, the tariffs applied, and other relevant indicators. It is updated regularly to reflect the most recent trade data."/>
