      <property key="skos:example"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="Public Tax Metadata is a crucial component of the tax system. It provides a comprehensive overview of the tax structure, including the types of taxes (income tax, sales tax, property tax, etc.), tax rates, tax brackets, tax exemptions, and tax revenues. This metadata is used by individuals, businesses, researchers, and policymakers to understand the tax system, comply with tax laws, analyze tax policies, and make informed decisions. It is also used by tax authorities to administer the tax system efficiently and effectively. Public Tax Metadata is usually available on the websites of tax authorities and other government agencies. It is often presented in a structured and standardized format, such as JSON or XML, to facilitate easy access, analysis, and use of the data."/>
