      <property key="skos:example" value="For instance, a tax authority could use the Catalogue of Harmonised Tax Data Ontologies to standardize the representation of tax data in its systems, thereby improving data consistency and facilitating data exchange with other tax authorities. Similarly, a tax software developer could use the catalogue to ensure that its software is able to interpret and process tax data in a standardized way, thereby enhancing interoperability with other systems and platforms."/>
