    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Tax base amounts registry" id="id-c1378da20b36453abd84db4aded4d7a7">
      <documentation>Definition: The Tax Base Amounts Registry is a comprehensive database that records all the taxable amounts for individuals, businesses, and other entities. It is a crucial tool for tax authorities to calculate the tax liabilities accurately and efficiently.

Source: Investopedia

Source reference: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tax-base.asp

Additional information: The Tax Base Amounts Registry is a critical component in the tax administration system. It includes all the taxable income, property, sales, and other taxable entities. The registry is updated regularly to reflect the current financial status of taxpayers. It is used by tax authorities to calculate the tax liabilities of individuals and businesses. The registry helps in ensuring tax compliance and preventing tax evasion. It also aids in the formulation of tax policies and strategies. The data in the registry is confidential and is protected by privacy laws.

Example: For example, if a business has a taxable income of $1 million, this amount will be recorded in the Tax Base Amounts Registry. The tax authority will then use this information to calculate the business's tax liability. Similarly, if an individual owns a property worth $500,000, this value will be recorded in the registry. The tax authority will use this data to calculate the property tax for the individual.

LOST view: SV-Datasets Catalogue [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TaxBaseAmountsRegistryDataObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataSetCatalogueDataObject

ABB name: egovera:TaxBaseAmountsRegistryDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-27

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TaxBaseAmountsRegistryDataObject

dct:title: Tax Base Amounts Registry

</documentation>
