    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Business Sector catalogue" id="id-c3c2a6c4fc3a4d60a515ad9da1670ebc">
      <documentation>Definition: The Business Sector Catalogue is a comprehensive database that provides detailed information about various sectors within the business industry. It includes data about the nature of businesses, their operations, market trends, and other relevant details.

Source: Investopedia

Source reference: https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/business-sector.asp

Additional information: The Business Sector Catalogue is a valuable resource for business professionals, researchers, and students alike. It provides a thorough understanding of different business sectors, including their characteristics, challenges, opportunities, and trends. The catalogue may cover a wide range of sectors, from manufacturing and services to technology and healthcare. It may also provide insights into the economic impact of these sectors, their contribution to GDP, employment rates, and more. The data in the catalogue can be used for various purposes, such as market analysis, business planning, investment decisions, academic research, and policy-making.

LOST view: SV-Dataset [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessSectorCatalogueDataObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataSetDataObject

ABB name: egovera:BusinessSectorCatalogueDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-27

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessSectorCatalogueDataObject

dct:title: (Business) Sector Catalogue

</documentation>
