    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Multimedia Object Metadata" id="id-e8ade15f9145402c8baa7ed553b92cce">
      <documentation>Definition: Multimedia Object Metadata refers to structured information that describes and provides context to multimedia assets such as images, videos, audio files, and other multimedia content. It includes attributes such as title, creator, date, format, resolution, duration, keywords, and other descriptive information that helps identify, organize, and retrieve multimedia assets. Multimedia Object Metadata plays a crucial role in enabling efficient search, discovery, and management of multimedia content in various applications and systems.

Source: W3C

Source reference: https://www.w3.org/standards/

LOST view: SV-Business Agnostic Metadata

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/MultimediaObjectMetadataDataObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataSetDataObject

ABB name: egovera:MultimediaObjectMetadataDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-01-16

</documentation>
