      <property key="skos:note" value="The catalogue of assets that can be confiscated is a legal document that outlines the types of assets that can be seized by law enforcement or other authorities under specific circumstances. These circumstances can include, but are not limited to, criminal activity, unpaid taxes, or other legal obligations. The catalogue provides a detailed description of each type of asset, including its legal definition and the conditions under which it can be confiscated. It is important to note that the laws regarding asset confiscation can vary significantly from one jurisdiction to another, and the catalogue should be used as a general guide rather than a definitive source of legal advice."/>
