  <folder name="Motivation" id="id-0dad48e7ab84448180018f23471397d2" type="motivation">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Assessment" name="JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base" id="id-113a636ce13c4ec685b4db5917220220">
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/JRCDataSpacesKnowledgeBaseAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/JRCDataSpacesKnowledgeBaseAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:JRCDataSpacesKnowledgeBaseAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base Assessment"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="The JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base is a digital platform developed by the Joint Research Centre (JRC) of the European Commission. It serves as a comprehensive resource for information related to data spaces, which are virtual environments where data is exchanged and shared. The Knowledge Base includes a wide range of materials such as reports, case studies, technical guides, and policy documents. It aims to support the development and implementation of data spaces by providing relevant and up-to-date information to stakeholders, including policymakers, researchers, and data professionals."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA Team research"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="The JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base is a comprehensive resource that provides access to various datasets and information related to different fields of study. Here are some examples:&#xA;&#xA;1. Agriculture and Rural Development: This data space includes information about crop yield, livestock production, agricultural practices, and rural development policies across different regions.&#xA;&#xA;2. Climate Change: This data space provides datasets related to climate change indicators, greenhouse gas emissions, climate models, and impacts of climate change on various sectors.&#xA;&#xA;3. Energy: This data space includes data on energy production, consumption, energy efficiency, renewable energy sources, and energy policies.&#xA;&#xA;4. Health and Food Safety: This data space provides information on food safety standards, health indicators, disease outbreaks, and health policies.&#xA;&#xA;5. Migration and Demography: This data space includes data on migration flows, population demographics, social integration, and policies related to migration and demography.&#xA;&#xA;6. Transport and Mobility: This data space provides datasets on transport networks, mobility patterns, transport emissions, and transport policies.&#xA;&#xA;7. Digital Economy: This data space includes information on digital technologies, internet usage, e-commerce, digital skills, and digital policies.&#xA;&#xA;8. Environment and Sustainability: This data space provides data on environmental indicators, biodiversity, waste management, water resources, and sustainability policies.&#xA;&#xA;9. Education and Culture: This data space includes data on education systems, cultural heritage, language diversity, and policies related to education and culture.&#xA;&#xA;10. Security and Justice: This data space provides information on crime rates, justice systems, security threats, and policies related to security and justice."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base is a comprehensive online resource developed by the Joint Research Centre (JRC) of the European Commission. It is designed to provide a wide range of information and resources related to data spaces, which are virtual environments where organizations can share, exchange, and work with data.&#xA;&#xA;The Knowledge Base is a part of the JRC's broader initiative to support the development and implementation of data spaces in Europe, in line with the European strategy for data. It aims to facilitate the understanding, design, and operation of data spaces by providing a variety of resources, including technical guides, policy documents, case studies, and research papers.&#xA;&#xA;The JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base covers a wide range of topics related to data spaces, including data governance, data interoperability, data infrastructure, and data sharing. It also provides information on various aspects of data spaces, such as their architecture, legal and ethical considerations, and potential applications in different sectors.&#xA;&#xA;The Knowledge Base is intended for a wide range of users, including policymakers, data professionals, researchers, and businesses. It aims to support these users in making informed decisions about the design and implementation of data spaces, and to promote the sharing and reuse of data in a secure and trustworthy manner.&#xA;&#xA;In addition to providing information and resources, the JRC Data Spaces Knowledge Base also serves as a platform for dialogue and collaboration. It encourages users to contribute their own knowledge and experiences, and to engage in discussions and collaborations with other users. This collaborative approach is intended to foster a vibrant and dynamic community of practice around data spaces, and to support the ongoing development and evolution of data spaces in Europe."/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="N/A"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Assessment" name="Data Spaces Business Alliance" id="id-14800a4ed9ed41cb99d1ceed658f9202">
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataSpacesBusinessAllianceAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataSpacesBusinessAllianceAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:DataSpacesBusinessAllianceAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Data Spaces Business Alliance Assessment"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="The Data Spaces Business Alliance is a global initiative launched by several leading technology companies, including Atos, Dell Technologies, Google Cloud, and IBM. The alliance aims to develop a set of standards, protocols, and best practices for data sharing and collaboration across industries. The goal is to create secure and trusted data spaces that enable businesses to share and leverage data in a privacy-compliant manner, fostering innovation and driving digital transformation."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA Team research"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="1. Snowflake and Databricks: Snowflake, a cloud-based data warehousing startup, and Databricks, a big data analytics service, have formed a business alliance to provide a unified, open, and dynamic data ecosystem. This alliance allows customers to run Databricks' analytics platform on Snowflake's data cloud, enabling them to easily unify, analyze, and extract valuable insights from their data.&#xA;&#xA;2. Google Cloud and SAP: Google Cloud and SAP have formed a business alliance to help customers execute business transformations, migrate critical business systems to the cloud, and augment existing business systems with Google Cloud capabilities in artificial intelligence and machine learning.&#xA;&#xA;3. Microsoft and Adobe: Microsoft and Adobe have formed a strategic partnership to redefine customer experiences. The partnership makes Adobe Marketing Cloud the preferred marketing service for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Enterprise edition.&#xA;&#xA;4. IBM and Salesforce: IBM and Salesforce have partnered to deliver joint solutions designed to leverage artificial intelligence and enable companies to make smarter decisions, faster. The partnership brings together IBM Watson and Salesforce Einstein to enable an entirely new level of intelligent customer engagement across sales, service, marketing, commerce and more.&#xA;&#xA;5. Amazon Web Services and Tableau: Tableau, a leading data visualization tool, has partnered with Amazon Web Services to provide a comprehensive cloud-based analytics solution. This partnership allows users to connect, visualize, and share data with a seamless experience from the source in AWS to the visualization in Tableau.&#xA;&#xA;6. Oracle and VMware: Oracle and VMware have formed a strategic partnership to support customers’ hybrid cloud strategies and enable them to leverage their existing software investments while enjoying new technology advancements. This partnership allows customers to run, manage, connect, and secure applications across VMware environments and Oracle Cloud Infrastructure.&#xA;&#xA;7. Cisco and NetApp: Cisco and NetApp have formed a business alliance to deliver a portfolio of integrated solutions designed to simplify and modernize IT and deliver enhanced data management capabilities. The partnership combines the innovation of Cisco UCS Integrated Infrastructure with the simplicity of NetApp data services."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Data Spaces Business Alliance is a global initiative established by a group of leading technology companies, including Atos, Dell Technologies, Google Cloud, IBM, Intel, Microsoft, and SAP. The alliance aims to create a trusted and secure data sharing environment that enables businesses to collaborate and innovate through shared data spaces. &#xA;&#xA;The Data Spaces Business Alliance is built on the principle of data sovereignty, which means that organizations maintain control over their data, even when it is shared or combined with data from other organizations. This is achieved through the use of secure and standardized technologies that ensure data privacy and security.&#xA;&#xA;The alliance's goal is to create a global standard for data spaces, which are virtual environments where organizations can share and collaborate on data. These data spaces are designed to be interoperable, meaning that they can work together seamlessly, regardless of the technology or platform used.&#xA;&#xA;The Data Spaces Business Alliance also aims to foster a vibrant ecosystem of technology providers, data providers, and data users. This ecosystem will support the development and adoption of data spaces, and will provide businesses with the tools and resources they need to leverage shared data for innovation and growth.&#xA;&#xA;The alliance believes that by enabling secure and trusted data sharing, it can help businesses unlock new opportunities, drive innovation, and create value. This could include developing new products and services, improving operational efficiency, or gaining insights for decision-making.&#xA;&#xA;In summary, the Data Spaces Business Alliance is a global initiative that aims to create a secure and trusted environment for data sharing, based on the principle of data sovereignty. It seeks to establish a global standard for data spaces, foster a vibrant ecosystem of stakeholders, and help businesses unlock the value of shared data."/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="N/A"/>
    </element>
