    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 19 October 2022" id="id-0ab374e224194459a80ae38cee35c083">
      <documentation>Description: Regulation (EU) 2022/2065, also known as the Digital Service Act (DSA), updates the European Union's legal framework for illegal content on intermediaries, in particular by modernising the e-Commerce Directive adopted in 2000. In doing so, the DSA aims to harmonise different national laws in the European Union that have emerged at national level to address illegal content.

Publisher: EUR-Lex

Source: http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj

