    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="European legal act on the holding and movement of products subject to excise duty" id="id-e1ab05142d1c421487d74b4554f15552">
      <documentation>DESCRIPTION:&#xD;
&quot;European Legal act introducing arrangements for products subject to excise duty in order to guarantee their free circulation and therefore the proper functioning of the EU’s single market.
&quot;</documentation>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:spatial" value="EU"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2008/118/oj"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="European legal act on the holding and movement of products subject to excise duty"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="Council Directive 2008/118/EC is a European legal act that concerns the general arrangements for products subject to excise duties, and the holding, movement, and monitoring of such products. It applies to alcohol, alcoholic beverages, energy products, electricity, and tobacco products. The directive aims to ensure the proper functioning of the internal market and a high level of health protection."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="EUR-Lex"/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/ALL/?uri=CELEX%3A32008L0118"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="For example, a company producing alcoholic beverages in France must comply with the regulations set out in this directive when transporting their products to a different EU member state, such as Germany. They must ensure that the excise duty is paid in Germany, where the products are consumed. They must also use the computerised system to monitor the movement of their products."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The directive establishes the conditions under which products subject to excise duty can be produced, held, received and transported. It also provides for a computerised system for monitoring the movement of these products to ensure that excise is paid in the member state where the products are consumed. The directive also sets out the procedures for payment and reimbursement of excise duty in cross-border situations."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Binding Power and Jurisdiction"/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Legal"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="taxes"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BindingInstrumentRequirement"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Data Act Proposal" id="id-e4269c27d0f549a1b7e39ccfb5830ae1">
      <documentation>Description: The Digital Services Act is a regulation passed by the European Parliament and Council that aims to create a single market for digital services in the European Union. The act amends Directive 2000/31/EC and introduces new rules for online platforms, including requirements for transparency, accountability, and content moderation. It also establishes a new regulatory framework for digital services, including provisions for data protection, cybersecurity, and consumer protection. The act is designed to promote innovation and competition in the digital economy while ensuring that online platforms operate in a responsible and accountable manner.

Publisher: EUR-Lex

Source: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52022PC0068

Last modification: 26/06/2023

EIRA traceability: eira:BindingInstrumentRequirement

LOST view: Legal view - Binding Power and Jurisdiction

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Additional identifier: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52022PC0068

Title: Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL on harmonised rules on fair access to and use of data (Data Act)

</documentation>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:52022PC0068"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL on harmonised rules on fair access to and use of data (Data Act)"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The Digital Services Act is a regulation passed by the European Parliament and Council that aims to create a single market for digital services in the European Union. The act amends Directive 2000/31/EC and introduces new rules for online platforms, including requirements for transparency, accountability, and content moderation. It also establishes a new regulatory framework for digital services, including provisions for data protection, cybersecurity, and consumer protection. The act is designed to promote innovation and competition in the digital economy while ensuring that online platforms operate in a responsible and accountable manner."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="EUR-Lex"/>
