    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="National Schema on unemployment insurance" id="id-fc3f5f979b2e4baf96b18dbf13608fdc">
      <documentation>DESCRIPTION:&#xD;
National legal act  that allows the government to tax businesses for the purpose of collecting revenue that is then allocated to state unemployment agencies and paid to unemployed workers who are eligible to claim unemployment insurance.&#xD;
</documentation>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:spatial" value="National"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/NationalSchemaOnUnemploymentInsuranceRequirement"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="National Schema on unemployment insurance"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="For instance, in Germany, the national regulation on unemployment insurance is managed by the Federal Employment Agency. Unemployed individuals who have paid into the unemployment insurance system for at least 12 months in the last two years are eligible to receive benefits. The amount of benefits is based on the individual's previous earnings, and benefits can be received for up to 24 months, depending on the individual's age and length of employment history."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The regulation stipulates that each member state must have a system in place to provide unemployment benefits to eligible citizens. The specifics of these systems, such as the amount of benefits and the duration for which they are provided, are determined at the national level, within the framework of the EU's regulations. The regulation also requires member states to share information with each other about recipients of unemployment benefits, to prevent fraud and ensure that benefits are distributed fairly."/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="The national regulation on unemployment insurance within the member states of the European Union refers to the specific laws, rules, and guidelines established by each individual member state to implement and manage the European Union's overarching regulations on unemployment insurance. These national regulations are designed to provide financial support to citizens who are unemployed through no fault of their own, while they seek new employment."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="European Union"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference" value="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=LEGISSUM:c10416"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Binding Power and Jurisdiction"/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Legal"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:NationalSchemaOnUnemploymentInsuranceRequirement"/>
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/NationalSchemaOnUnemploymentInsuranceRequirement"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="taxes"/>
      <property key="skos:broader" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BindingInstrumentRequirement"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Stakeholder" name="Organisation" id="id-0f4f023733a242e095bd0e3d9b7e7b1f">
      <documentation>Definition: Organization ABB is a Stakeholder that corresponds to a collection of people organized together into a community or other social, commercial or political structure. The group has some common purpose or reason for existence which goes beyond the set of people belonging to it and can act as an Agent. Organizations are often decomposable into hierarchical structures.

Source: SEMIC-CPOV

Source reference: https://semiceu.github.io/CPOV/releases/2.1.0/#Organization

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Any instance of an organisation with a legal personality, e.g. a Business, a Public Organisation, a Consortium, an NGO, etc.

IoP Dimension: Behavioural IoP

LOST view: Organisational view

Interoperability saliency: The Organization ABB is relevant for behavioural and organizational interoperability because it permits the identification of procedures, stakeholders and intra-company frameworks that facilitate the exchange of data, information and knowledge between digital public services.

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/OrganisationStakeholder

eira:ID: ABB494

ABB name: eira:OrganisationStakeholder

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-12-01

</documentation>
