    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Shared Application Content" id="id-03aa81bff49e488d8e0b4bbd270eca22">
      <documentation>Definition: Shared Application Content ABB is a Grouping setting application (re)usable resources, with convergence power, for the enhancement of interoperability across digital platforms. It enables the sharing and integration of software tools and services, fostering collaborative functionality within and across applications to support the attainment of public policy goals.

Source: Inspired in referent cloud service providers definitions

Last modification: 2024-01-08

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SharedApplicationContentGrouping

LOST view: Technical view - application

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

ABB name: eira:SharedApplicationContentGrouping

Interoperability Saliency: The Shared Application Content ABB is a key interoperability enabler (*) for governance, behavioural and structural interoperability because it aggregates components to enable knowledge sharing across public administration to achieve their public policy goals.

Interoperability Dimension: Governance IoP

Viewpoint: Highlevel viewpoint

Additional identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SharedApplicationContentGrouping

EIF Layer: TechnicalApplication

</documentation>
