      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticDataFormatRepresentationAndSyntaxSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticDataFormatRepresentationAndSyntaxSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Business Agnostic Data Format, Representation And Syntax Solutions Catalogue"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:BusinessAgnosticDataFormatRepresentationAndSyntaxSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="Business Agnostic Data Format, Representation and Syntax Solutions (ABB) is a grouping that covers a wide range of technical specifications, standards, and formats designed to facilitate the representation, storage, and exchange of structured data in a machine-readable manner. These solutions are independent of specific business domains, making them applicable across various industries and use cases. They provide the necessary tools for businesses to create, integrate, and utilize structured data, promoting data interoperability and enabling the development of data-driven applications."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA Team Research"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="Examples of application of these solutions include: creating and sharing RDF data using Turtle format, representing and exchanging geospatial data using GeoJSON or KML, defining and exchanging code lists using Genericode, representing date and time information in a standardized format using ISO 8601, archiving relational databases using SIARD 2.0 format, and querying semantic data using SPARQL."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The elements contained within this grouping include various data models, markup languages, data representation methods, and data interchange formats, among others. They cover a broad spectrum of data-related aspects, including data modeling (Common Data Model), data representation (XML, CSV, JSON), date and time representation (ISO 8601), secure and reliable document exchange (AS4 Profile of ebMS 3.0 v1.0), database archiving (SIARD 2.0 format for databases), RDF serialization (RDF Serialisations, Turtle, RDF-XML, N3, NQuads, TRiG), knowledge organization (SKOS, SKOS-XL), linked data representation (JSON-LD, JSON-L), semantic web data formats (LDES, RDF, RDF-S, OWL2, RML, SPARQL*, RDF*, SPARQL), geospatial data formats (geoJSON, KML, GML), code list definition and exchange (Genericode), and SPARQL results representation (SPARQL-CSV)."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="SV-Functional Architecture Principles"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="Semantic view - Motivation"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="Semantic view"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Semantic"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Business Agnostic Forms Structure Catalogue" id="id-e5e06a246a954ca39677efed69d55696">
      <documentation>Definition: Business Agnostic Forms Structure Catalogue ABB is a grouping that covers a variety of form structures that are applicable across different business domains. These form structures are designed to be versatile and adaptable to various business needs, regardless of the industry or sector. The catalogue includes forms such as Contact Form, Feedback Form, Survey Form, Registration Form, and Order Form.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Business Agnostic Forms Structure Catalogue ABB is a comprehensive collection of form structures that are not specific to any business or industry. These forms are designed to be adaptable and versatile, allowing them to be used in a variety of different business contexts. The Contact Form is used for collecting basic information about a person or entity, the Feedback Form is used for gathering feedback or opinions, the Survey Form is used for conducting surveys or polls, the Registration Form is used for registering users or participants, and the Order Form is used for placing orders or making purchases. Each form structure can be customized to suit the specific needs of the business, making this catalogue a valuable resource for any business.

Example: Examples of application for the Business Agnostic Forms Structure Catalogue ABB could be a retail business using the Order Form for customers to place orders, a research institution using the Survey Form to conduct a study, a service provider using the Feedback Form to gather customer feedback, an event organizer using the Registration Form to register participants, or a company using the Contact Form on their website for visitors to get in touch.

LOST view: SV-Forms Structure

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticFormsStructureCatalogueGrouping

