            <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-8b571dc4eca6413996581fe86e14a0b9" font="1|Segoe UI|9.0|3|WINDOWS|1|0|0|0|0|700|1|0|0|1|0|0|0|0|Segoe UI" textPosition="1" archimateElement="id-58ee7a4f1e03458686c717fb34d551c0">
              <bounds x="2112" y="1332" width="250" height="75"/>
              <sourceConnection xsi:type="archimate:Connection" id="id-41914a1d7e07469b9649f7a5f7882877" source="id-8b571dc4eca6413996581fe86e14a0b9" target="id-81919fdd08b74522a3d8ce6bf437e762" archimateRelationship="id-448afe20eb3e46ef9bffa3c574007197"/>
            </child>
            <documentation>The Organizational-Functional Architecture Principles view is a crucial aspect of solutions architecture, as it directly influences the implementation of solutions within an organization's functional layers. This view focuses on aligning the design and implementation of solutions with the goals, requirements, and processes of the organization.&#xD;
&#xD;
Aligning the Organizational-Functional Architecture Principles view with the organizational building blocks brings several benefits. Firstly, it ensures consistency and coherence across different functional areas within the organization. By defining and adhering to architecture principles, solutions architects establish a standardized approach that allows for seamless integration and interoperability between various building blocks. This consistency fosters effective communication and collaboration among departments and teams, promoting efficient business processes and operations.&#xD;
&#xD;
Secondly, aligning the Organizational-Functional Architecture Principles view supports the scalability and adaptability of solutions. The architecture principles provide guidelines for designing modular, flexible, and reusable solutions. By considering the specific requirements and characteristics of each organizational building block, solutions architects can design solutions that can easily accommodate future changes and expansions. This scalability and adaptability enable the organization to respond to evolving business needs, reducing the time and resources required for future modifications.&#xD;
&#xD;
Furthermore, aligning the Organizational-Functional Architecture Principles view enhances governance and decision-making processes within the organization. The architecture principles serve as a reference for making design decisions, ensuring that solutions align with the strategic objectives and priorities of the organization. By considering the unique characteristics and requirements of each building block, solutions architects can make informed choices that optimize resource utilization and support the overall organizational strategy.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
