            <documentation>NARRATIVE:
The TVI-Application Integration Infrastructure Enablers [Motivation] view extends Technical view - infrastructure and provides a comprehensive framework for leveraging various elements that facilitate the integration of disparate applications and systems within an organization. 

The view is divided into several groupings, each containing elements that serve specific functions. The first grouping is the &quot;Application Integration Infrastructure Enablers&quot;, which includes technology services such as the Enterprise Service Bus, API Manager, GraphQL Server, Serverless Orchestrator, Application Server, Event Manager, and API Gateway. These services enable the integration between applications by performing various tasks such as data transformation, connectivity handling, message routing, communication protocol conversion, and managing the composition of multiple requests.

The second grouping is &quot;API Enablers&quot;, which refers to components and frameworks that support the implementation and cataloguing of software interfaces. This includes application components like the Service Registry and API Catalogue, and application interfaces such as Web Service, API, ePayment, eInvoicing, eTendering, eProfessional Qualification, Geo-Localization, eProcurement, Supply Chain Management, eQualification, eNotification, ERP System, Financial Management, Log Management, Service Discovery and Registry, API Discovery and Catalogue, and Service Registry.

The third grouping is &quot;Content Delivery Infrastructure Enablers&quot;, which includes technology services like the Web Server and Streaming Server. These services enable the delivery of digital content such as web pages, videos, images, and audio files to end-users.

The fourth grouping is &quot;Management Infrastructure Enablers&quot;, which includes technology services like Logger, Audit Manager, Telemetry, and Management Console. These services enable the efficient management of a public administration's IT platforms.

The final grouping is &quot;Dataspace Enablers&quot;, which includes application services like Dataspace, Dataspace Connector, Dataspace Connector Consumer, and Dataspace Connector Provider. These services support the creation and management of a dataspace, enabling the integration, transformation, and availability of data.

Each of these elements plays a crucial role in the overall application integration infrastructure, contributing to the efficient and effective functioning of an organization's IT systems. The motivation behind this view is to provide a comprehensive framework that facilitates the integration of disparate applications and systems, thereby enhancing the organization's operational efficiency and effectiveness.
</documentation>
          </element>
